  "description": "Dominant Markov-trace channel analysis for β_EW Δ_I^minimal at n=6. Decomposes tr_M = Σ y_λ χ_λ via canonical 50-dps Wenzl-bridge y_λ + float64 Hoefsmit χ_λ; identifies which Wedderburn block dominates the trace. Scans each block's internal eigenvalue ratios for the closest match to z_markov = 1/(√q+1/√q). Finding: the (5,1) block dominates (43% of |tr_M|) and has z_markov as an internal ratio to 0.5%, matching the PL SDP's identification of a_PL = z_markov (commit 5e7459cf0). The (3,2,1) staircase block — the target of the original conj:staircase-ew-residual — contributes only 0.9% to tr_M. Suggests the EW reading should be REFINED to target the dominant (Markov-trace-dominant) channel, not the staircase channel.",
